{"task_id": "HumanEval/2", "solution": "```python\ndef truncate_number(number: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Given a positive floating-point number, return its decimal part.\n    The number is decomposed into an integer part and the leftover decimal component.\n    >>> truncate_number(3.5)\n    0.5\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(number, float):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a float.\")\n    \n    if number < 0:\n        # Handles negative numbers by returning the absolute value of their decimal part.\n        # This aligns with a common interpretation for \"decimal part\" for non-positive input.\n        return truncate_number(abs(number))\n\n    integer_part = int(number)\n    decimal_part = number - integer_part\n    return decimal_part\n```"}
