{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "```python\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"Input are two strings a and b consisting only of 1s and 0s.\n    Perform binary XOR on these inputs and return result also as a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate that inputs are non-empty and contain only '0's and '1's.\n    for s_name, s_value in [('a', a), ('b', b)]:\n        if not s_value:\n            raise ValueError(f\"Input string '{s_name}' cannot be empty.\")\n        if not all(c in '01' for c in s_value):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Input string '{s_name}' must contain only '0's and '1's.\")\n\n    # Pad the shorter string with leading zeros to match the length of the longer string.\n    max_len = max(len(a), len(b))\n    a_padded = a.zfill(max_len)\n    b_padded = b.zfill(max_len)\n\n    # Perform bitwise XOR operation character by character.\n    result = []\n    for i in range(max_len):\n        bit_a = int(a_padded[i])\n        bit_b = int(b_padded[i])\n        xor_result = bit_a ^ bit_b\n        result.append(str(xor_result))\n    return \"\".join(result)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/10", "solution": "```python\ndef is_palindrome(string: str) -> bool:\n    \"\"\" Test if given string is a palindrome.\n    Compares the input string with its reverse to verify palindromic property.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    return string == string[::-1]\n\n\ndef make_palindrome(string: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Find the shortest palindrome that begins with a supplied string.\n    Identifies the longest palindromic suffix and appends the reversed preceding prefix.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(string, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not string:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Iterate from the full string length down to 1 to find the longest palindromic suffix.\n    for i in range(len(string), 0, -1):\n        suffix = string[len(string) - i:]\n        if is_palindrome(suffix):\n            # The prefix before the longest palindromic suffix is reversed and appended.\n            prefix_to_reverse = string[:len(string) - i]\n            return string + prefix_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/11", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n\nclass InvalidBinaryStringError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid binary string input.\n    Raised if a string contains characters other than '0' or '1'.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\nclass UnequalLengthError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for binary strings of unequal length.\n    Raised if two strings required to be of equal length are not.\n    \"\"\"\n    pass\n\n\ndef string_xor(a: str, b: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs binary XOR on two strings a and b consisting only of 1s and 0s.\n    Returns the result also as a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # FR1: Validate that input strings 'a' and 'b' contain only '0's and '1's.\n    if not all(c in '01' for c in a):\n        raise InvalidBinaryStringError(f\"Input string '{a}' contains non-binary characters.\")\n    if not all(c in '01' for c in b):\n        raise InvalidBinaryStringError(f\"Input string '{b}' contains non-binary characters.\")\n\n    # FR2: Validate that input strings 'a' and 'b' are of equal length.\n    if len(a) != len(b):\n        raise UnequalLengthError(f\"Input strings must be of equal length. Got {len(a)} and {len(b)}.\")\n\n    # FR3: Perform bitwise XOR operation on corresponding characters.\n    result_chars: List[str] = []\n    for i in range(len(a)):\n        result_chars.append('0' if a[i] == b[i] else '1')\n    \n    # FR4: Return the XOR result as a single string.\n    return \"\".join(result_chars)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\n\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Out of list of strings, return the longest one. Returns the first one in case of a tie.\n    Returns None if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    longest_str_found = None\n    max_length_found = -1\n\n    for s in strings:\n        current_length = len(s)\n        if current_length > max_length_found:\n            max_length_found = current_length\n            longest_str_found = s\n\n    return longest_str_found\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/12", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List, Optional\n\n\ndef longest(strings: List[str]) -> Optional[str]:\n    \"\"\" Out of list of strings, return the longest one.\n    Returns the first one in case of multiple strings of the same length, or None if the list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not strings:\n        return None\n\n    longest_str = \"\"\n    max_length = -1\n\n    for s in strings:\n        if len(s) > max_length:\n            max_length = len(s)\n            longest_str = s\n    return longest_str\n```"}
