{"task_id": "HumanEval/15", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input. Inherits from ValueError.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\nclass InputValidator:\n    \"\"\"Utility for validating inputs.\"\"\"\n\n    def validate_non_negative_integer(self, n: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if 'n' is a non-negative integer.\n        Raises InvalidInputError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(n, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be an integer.\")\n        if n < 0:\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\nclass StringSequenceGenerator:\n    \"\"\"Generates a space-delimited string of numbers from 0 to n.\"\"\"\n\n    def __init__(self):\n        \"\"\"Initializes with an InputValidator instance.\"\"\"\n        self.validator = InputValidator()\n\n    def generate_sequence(self, n: int) -> str:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns a space-delimited string of numbers from 0 to n.\n        Raises InvalidInputError for invalid 'n'.\n        \"\"\"\n        self.validator.validate_non_negative_integer(n)\n\n        if n == 0:\n            return '0'\n\n        return ' '.join(str(i) for i in range(n + 1))\n\ndef string_sequence(n: int) -> str:\n    \"\"\" Return a string containing space-delimited numbers starting from 0 upto n inclusive.\n    >>> string_sequence(0)\n    '0'\n    >>> string_sequence(5)\n    '0 1 2 3 4 5'\n    \"\"\"\n    generator = StringSequenceGenerator()\n    return generator.generate_sequence(n)\n```\n"}
