{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n# Define the note-to-beat mapping as a constant.\n# This aligns with the 'NoteType' conceptual class attributes from the design.\nNOTE_BEAT_MAP = {\n    \"o\": 4,   # Whole note\n    \"o|\": 2,  # Half note\n    \".|\": 1   # Quarter note\n}\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string representing musical notes in a special ASCII format.\n    Your task is to parse this string and return list of integers corresponding to how many beats does each\n    not last.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handle empty input string (FR1 error handling).\n    if not music_string:\n        return []\n\n    # Split the string into individual note symbols (FR1 main flow).\n    # The .split() method correctly handles strings with only spaces, resulting in an empty list.\n    notes = music_string.split()\n    beat_durations: List[int] = []\n\n    # Iterate through each note symbol to determine its beat duration.\n    for note_symbol in notes:\n        # Map note symbols to beats; unknown symbols are ignored (FR2 main flow & error handling).\n        beats = NOTE_BEAT_MAP.get(note_symbol)\n        if beats is not None:\n            beat_durations.append(beats) # Aggregate valid beat durations.\n    \n    # Return the aggregated list of beat durations (FR3 postconditions).\n    return beat_durations\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/17", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import List\n\n# Maps musical notation symbols to their corresponding beat durations.\n_NOTE_MAP = {\n    \"o\": 4,   # Whole note.\n    \"o|\": 2,  # Half note.\n    \".|\": 1   # Quarter note.\n}\n\ndef parse_music(music_string: str) -> List[int]:\n    \"\"\" Input to this function is a string representing musical notes in a special ASCII format.\n    Your task is to parse this string and return list of integers corresponding to how many beats does each\n    not last.\n\n    Here is a legend:\n    'o' - whole note, lasts four beats\n    'o|' - half note, lasts two beats\n    '.|' - quater note, lasts one beat\n\n    >>> parse_music('o o| .| o| o| .| .| .| .| o o')\n    [4, 2, 1, 2, 2, 1, 1, 1, 1, 4, 4]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Handles empty or purely whitespace input string as per FR1 and error handling.\n    if not music_string.strip():\n        return []\n\n    beats = []\n    # Splits the input string by spaces to process each note symbol.\n    note_symbols = music_string.split(' ')\n    for symbol in note_symbols:\n        # Adds the beat duration to the result if the symbol is recognized in the map.\n        if symbol in _NOTE_MAP:\n            beats.append(_NOTE_MAP[symbol])\n    return beats\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/18", "solution": "```python\ndef how_many_times(string: str, substring: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds substring occurrences in a string, counting overlaps.\n    Returns the total count, or 0 if strings are empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not substring or not string:\n        return 0\n\n    count = 0\n    start_index = 0\n    while True:\n        index = string.find(substring, start_index)\n        if index != -1:\n            count += 1\n            start_index = index + 1\n        else:\n            break\n    return count\n```"}
