{"task_id": "HumanEval/37", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_even(l: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"This function sorts elements at even indices in a list, preserving odd-indexed elements.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    if not l:\n        return []\n\n    even_elements = [l[i] for i in range(0, len(l), 2)]\n    try:\n        even_elements.sort()\n    except TypeError as e:\n        raise TypeError(f\"Elements at even indices are not sortable: {e}\") from e\n\n    result = l[:]  # Create a shallow copy to preserve odd elements.\n    even_idx_counter = 0\n    for i in range(0, len(l), 2):\n        result[i] = even_elements[even_idx_counter]\n        even_idx_counter += 1\n    \n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    takes as input string encoded with encode_cyclic function. Returns decoded string.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Split the input string into groups of three characters.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n\n    # For each group, reverse the cyclic shift if its length is 3.\n    decoded_groups = [(group[-1] + group[:-1]) if len(group) == 3 else group for group in groups]\n\n    # Join the processed groups back into a single string.\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/38", "solution": "```python\ndef decode_cyclic(s: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Decodes a string previously encoded by the encode_cyclic function.\n    It reverses the cyclic shift applied to groups of three characters.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n    if not s:\n        return \"\"\n\n    # Split the input string into groups of three characters.\n    groups = [s[(3 * i):min((3 * i + 3), len(s))] for i in range((len(s) + 2) // 3)]\n\n    # Reverse the cyclic shift for each group of length three.\n    decoded_groups = []\n    for group in groups:\n        if len(group) == 3:\n            # If 'g0g1g2' was encoded to 'g1g2g0', then 'g1g2g0' decodes to 'g0g1g2'.\n            # This is achieved by taking the last char and prepending it to the first two.\n            decoded_group = group[2] + group[0:2]\n            decoded_groups.append(decoded_group)\n        else:\n            # Groups with fewer than three elements remain unchanged.\n            decoded_groups.append(group)\n\n    return \"\".join(decoded_groups)\n```"}
