{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Converts a non-negative integer x (base 10) to its string representation\n    in the specified target base. Raises ValueError if base is invalid or x is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not (2 <= base <= 9):\n        raise ValueError(\"Base must be between 2 and 9.\")\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input number x must be non-negative.\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    digits = []\n    while x > 0:\n        remainder = x % base\n        digits.append(str(remainder))\n        x //= base\n\n    digits.reverse()\n    return \"\".join(digits)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/45", "solution": "```python\ndef triangle_area(a, h):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the area of a triangle given its base and height.\n    Raises ValueError for non-numeric or negative inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, (int, float)) or a < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Base 'a' must be a non-negative numerical value.\")\n    if not isinstance(h, (int, float)) or h < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Height 'h' must be a non-negative numerical value.\")\n\n    area = 0.5 * a * h\n    return float(area)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/44", "solution": "```python\ndef change_base(x: int, base: int):\n    \"\"\"Change numerical base of input number x to base.\n    return string representation after the conversion.\n    base numbers are less than 10.\n    >>> change_base(8, 3)\n    '22'\n    >>> change_base(8, 2)\n    '1000'\n    >>> change_base(7, 2)\n    '111'\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int) or x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'x' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(base, int) or not (2 <= base <= 9):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'base' must be an integer between 2 and 9 (inclusive).\")\n\n    if x == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    result_digits = []\n    current_x = x\n    while current_x > 0:\n        remainder = current_x % base\n        result_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        current_x //= base\n\n    return \"\".join(result_digits[::-1])\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/45", "solution": "```python\ndef triangle_area(a, h):\n    \"\"\"Given length of a side and high return area for a triangle.\n    >>> triangle_area(5, 3)\n    7.5\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(a, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"a must be a number.\")\n    if a <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"a must be a positive number.\")\n\n    if not isinstance(h, (int, float)):\n        raise TypeError(\"h must be a number.\")\n    if h <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"h must be a positive number.\")\n\n    return 0.5 * a * h\n```"}
