{"task_id": "HumanEval/49", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef modp(n: int, p: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Return 2^n modulo p.\n    Validates inputs and calculates using modular exponentiation by squaring.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n < 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Exponent 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n    if not isinstance(p, int) or p <= 0:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Modulus 'p' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    base = 2\n    res = 1\n    base %= p\n\n    while n > 0:\n        if n % 2 == 1:\n            res = (res * base) % p\n        base = (base * base) % p\n        n //= 2\n    return res\n```"}
