{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\ndef monotonic(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Raises TypeError for invalid input types or non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(l, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    for item in l:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise TypeError(\"List elements must be numbers.\")\n\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    def _is_increasing_internal(arr: list) -> bool:\n        # Handles empty/single-element lists as per FR1.\n        if len(arr) <= 1:\n            return True\n        for i in range(len(arr) - 1):\n            if arr[i] > arr[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_decreasing_internal(arr: list) -> bool:\n        # Handles empty/single-element lists as per FR2.\n        if len(arr) <= 1:\n            return True\n        for i in range(len(arr) - 1):\n            if arr[i] < arr[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    return _is_increasing_internal(l) or _is_decreasing_internal(l)\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/57", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the monotonic function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef monotonic(l: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Return True if list elements are monotonically increasing or decreasing.\n    Raises InvalidInputError for non-list or non-numeric inputs.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _validate_input(l_param: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that input is a list of numbers.\"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(l_param, list):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n        for item in l_param:\n            if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n                raise InvalidInputError(\"List elements must be numbers (int or float).\")\n\n    def _is_increasing(l_param: list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the list is non-decreasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(l_param) - 1):\n            if l_param[i] > l_param[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    def _is_decreasing(l_param: list) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if the list is non-increasing.\"\"\"\n        for i in range(len(l_param) - 1):\n            if l_param[i] < l_param[i+1]:\n                return False\n        return True\n\n    _validate_input(l)\n\n    if len(l) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    return _is_increasing(l) or _is_decreasing(l)\n```"}
