{"task_id": "HumanEval/61", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input.\n    Used when the input to bracket validation is not a string.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef correct_bracketing(brackets: str):\n    \"\"\" brackets is a string of \"(\" and \")\".\n    return True if every opening bracket has a corresponding closing bracket.\n\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(\")\n    False\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"()\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\"(()())\")\n    True\n    >>> correct_bracketing(\")(()\")\n    False\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(brackets, str):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input 'brackets' must be a string.\")\n\n    count = 0\n    for char in brackets:\n        if char == '(':\n            count += 1\n        elif char == ')':\n            count -= 1\n        # If count drops below zero, a closing bracket appeared without a preceding open one.\n        if count < 0:\n            return False\n    # For correct bracketing, the final count must be zero.\n    return count == 0\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\ndef derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the derivative of a polynomial represented by xs, where xs[i] is the coefficient of x^i.\n    Returns the derivative polynomial's coefficients in the same form.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not xs:\n        return []\n    # The derivative of c_i * x^i is i * c_i * x^(i-1).\n    # The constant term (x^0) disappears, so we start from the x^1 coefficient.\n    return [i * coeff for i, coeff in enumerate(xs[1:], start=1)]\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/62", "solution": "```python\ndef derivative(xs: list):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the derivative of a polynomial represented by coefficients.\n    The input list `xs` represents `xs[0] + xs[1]*x + xs[2]*x^2 + ....`\n    >>> derivative([3, 1, 2, 4, 5])\n    [1, 4, 12, 20]\n    >>> derivative([1, 2, 3])\n    [2, 6]\n    \"\"\"\n    # Validate input type and content.\n    if not isinstance(xs, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Coefficients must be a list.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(c, (int, float)) for c in xs):\n        raise ValueError(\"All coefficients must be numeric.\")\n\n    # Convert all coefficients to float for consistent calculation.\n    coefficients_float = [float(c) for c in xs]\n\n    # Handle empty and constant polynomials.\n    if len(coefficients_float) <= 1:\n        return []\n\n    # Calculate derivative coefficients using the power rule.\n    derived_coefficients = []\n    for i in range(1, len(coefficients_float)):\n        derived_coefficients.append(coefficients_float[i] * i)\n\n    return derived_coefficients\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "```python\n_fibfib_memo = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int):\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence efficiently using memoization.\n    It follows the definition: fibfib(0)=0, fibfib(1)=0, fibfib(2)=1, and fibfib(n)=fibfib(n-1)+fibfib(n-2)+fibfib(n-3) for n>2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n in _fibfib_memo:\n        return _fibfib_memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _fibfib_memo[n] = result\n    return result\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/63", "solution": "# Global dictionary for memoization to store previously computed FibFib numbers.\n_fibfib_memo = {}\n\ndef fibfib(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the n-th element of the FibFib number sequence using memoization.\n    Raises ValueError for negative input 'n'.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n in _fibfib_memo:\n        return _fibfib_memo[n]\n\n    if n == 0:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 1:\n        result = 0\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        # Recursively compute and sum the previous three FibFib numbers.\n        result = fibfib(n - 1) + fibfib(n - 2) + fibfib(n - 3)\n\n    _fibfib_memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/64", "solution": "```python\ndef vowels_count(s):\n    \"\"\"Counts vowels in a string, where 'y' is a vowel only if it's the last character.\n    Vowel counting is case-insensitive for 'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'.\n    \"\"\"\n    STANDARD_VOWELS = {'a', 'e', 'i', 'o', 'u'}\n    vowel_count = 0\n    s_lower = s.lower()\n\n    if not s_lower:\n        return 0\n\n    # Count standard vowels in all characters except the last one\n    for char in s_lower[:-1]:\n        if char in STANDARD_VOWELS:\n            vowel_count += 1\n\n    # Check the last character for 'y' special rule\n    if s_lower[-1] == 'y':\n        vowel_count += 1\n\n    return vowel_count\n```"}
