{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 1)\n    \"21\"\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 2)\n    \"12\"\n    \"\"\"\n    s_x = str(x)\n    n = len(s_x)\n\n    if shift > n:\n        # Reverses the digits if shift exceeds the number of digits.\n        return s_x[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Performs a right circular shift by the effective amount.\n        effective_shift = shift % n\n        return s_x[n - effective_shift:] + s_x[:n - effective_shift]\n```"}
