{"task_id": "HumanEval/65", "solution": "```python\ndef circular_shift(x, shift):\n    \"\"\"Circular shift the digits of the integer x, shift the digits right by shift\n    and return the result as a string.\n    If shift > number of digits, return digits reversed.\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 1)\n    \"21\"\n    >>> circular_shift(12, 2)\n    \"12\"\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(x, int) or not isinstance(shift, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs 'x' and 'shift' must be integers.\")\n    if x < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'x' must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    digits_str = str(x)\n    num_digits = len(digits_str)\n\n    if num_digits == 0:\n        return \"\"\n\n    if shift > num_digits:\n        return digits_str[::-1]\n    else:\n        # Calculate effective shift for right circular shift.\n        effective_shift = shift % num_digits\n        return digits_str[-effective_shift:] + digits_str[:-effective_shift]\n\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/66", "solution": "```python\ndef digitSum(s):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of ASCII values for uppercase English alphabet characters in a string.\n    Raises TypeError if the input is not a string.\"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(s, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input 's' must be a string.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for char in s:\n        # Check if the character is an uppercase English alphabet character (A-Z)\n        if 'A' <= char <= 'Z':\n            total_sum += ord(char)\n    return total_sum\n```"}
