{"task_id": "HumanEval/86", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef anti_shuffle(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns a string where characters within each word are sorted by ASCII value.\n    The original order of words and blank spaces is preserved.\n    \"\"\"\n    parts = re.split(r'(\\s+)', s)\n    processed_parts = []\n    for part in parts:\n        if part.strip():  # If the part contains non-space characters, it's a word.\n            processed_parts.append(\"\".join(sorted(part)))\n        else:  # Otherwise, it's a sequence of spaces or an empty string.\n            processed_parts.append(part)\n    return \"\".join(processed_parts)\n```"}
