{"task_id": "HumanEval/91", "solution": "```python\n    import re\n\ndef is_bored(S):\n    \"\"\"\n    You'll be given a string of words, and your task is to count the number\n    of boredoms. A boredom is a sentence that starts with the word \"I\".\n    Sentences are delimited by '.', '?' or '!'.\n   \n    For example:\n    >>> is_bored(\"Hello world\")\n    0\n    >>> is_bored(\"The sky is blue. The sun is shining. I love this weather\")\n    1\n    \"\"\"\n    if not S:\n        return 0\n\n    # Split the text into sentences using regex, keeping delimiters and handling whitespace.\n    sentences = re.split(r'(?<=[.?!])\\s*', S)\n    \n    # Filter out empty strings and strip whitespace from each potential sentence.\n    processed_sentences = [s.strip() for s in sentences if s.strip()]\n\n    boredom_count = 0\n    for sentence in processed_sentences:\n        # Check if the sentence starts with the word \"I\" (case-sensitive).\n        if sentence.startswith(\"I \") or sentence == \"I\":\n            boredom_count += 1\n            \n    return boredom_count\n```\n"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/88", "solution": "```python\ndef sort_array(array):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given an array of non-negative integers, return a copy of the given array after sorting.\n    Sorts in ascending order if sum(first, last) is odd, descending if even.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _is_non_negative_integer_local(value: any) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"Checks if a value is a non-negative integer.\n        Returns True if value is a non-negative integer, False otherwise.\n        \"\"\"\n        return isinstance(value, int) and value >= 0\n\n    def validate_array_elements_local(arr: list) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Validates that the input is a list and all its elements are non-negative integers.\n        Raises ValueError if validation fails.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not isinstance(arr, list):\n            raise ValueError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n        for element in arr:\n            if not _is_non_negative_integer_local(element):\n                raise ValueError(\"All elements in the array must be non-negative integers.\")\n\n    def _determine_sort_order_local(arr_to_check: list[int]) -> str:\n        \"\"\"Determines the sorting order based on the sum of the first and last elements.\n        Assumes array has at least two elements and is already validated.\n        \"\"\"\n        first_element = arr_to_check[0]\n        last_element = arr_to_check[len(arr_to_check) - 1]\n\n        if (first_element + last_element) % 2 != 0:\n            return \"ascending\"\n        else:\n            return \"descending\"\n\n    validate_array_elements_local(array)\n\n    if not array:\n        return []\n\n    if len(array) == 1:\n        return array[:]\n\n    sorted_copy = array[:]\n\n    sort_order = _determine_sort_order_local(array)\n\n    if sort_order == \"ascending\":\n        sorted_copy.sort()\n    else:\n        sorted_copy.sort(reverse=True)\n\n    return sorted_copy\n```"}
