{"task_id": "HumanEval/121", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(ValueError):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input parameters.\"\"\"\n    pass\n\ndef solution(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers, return the sum of all of the odd elements that are in even positions.\n    Input must be a non-empty list of integers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(lst, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not lst:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input list cannot be empty.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i, num in enumerate(lst):\n        if not isinstance(num, int):\n            raise InvalidInputError(f\"List element at index {i} is not an integer: {num}\")\n        if i % 2 == 0 and num % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += num\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/122", "solution": "```python\ndef add_elements(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a non-empty array of integers arr and an integer k, return\n    the sum of the elements with at most two digits from the first k elements of arr.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def is_two_digit(num: int) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Checks if an integer has at most two digits (i.e., its absolute value is less than 100).\n        \"\"\"\n        return -99 <= num <= 99\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Constraints ensure 1 <= k <= len(arr), so arr[0:k] is always valid.\n    for i in range(k):\n        element = arr[i]\n        if is_two_digit(element):\n            total_sum += element\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/121", "solution": "```python\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input to the solution function.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef solution(lst):\n    \"\"\"Given a non-empty list of integers, return the sum of all of the odd elements that are in even positions.\n\n    Examples\n    solution([5, 8, 7, 1]) ==> 12\n    solution([3, 3, 3, 3, 3]) ==> 9\n    solution([30, 13, 24, 321]) ==>0\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(lst, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n    if not lst:\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"List must be non-empty.\")\n    if not all(isinstance(x, int) for x in lst):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"List must contain only integers.\")\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(0, len(lst), 2):\n        element = lst[i]\n        if element % 2 != 0:\n            total_sum += element\n    return total_sum\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/123", "solution": "```python\ndef get_odd_collatz(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given a positive integer n, return a sorted list that has the odd numbers in collatz sequence.\n    The sequence terminates when 1 is reached, and the returned list contains unique odd numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(n, int) or n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    sequence = []\n    current = n\n    while True:\n        sequence.append(current)\n        if current == 1:\n            break\n        if current % 2 == 0:\n            current //= 2\n        else:\n            current = 3 * current + 1\n    \n    odd_numbers = {num for num in sequence if num % 2 != 0}\n    return sorted(list(odd_numbers))\n```"}
