{"task_id": "HumanEval/126", "solution": "```python\nfrom collections import Counter\n\ndef is_sorted(lst):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a list of non-negative integers is sorted ascendingly\n    and if no number appears more than twice. Returns True if valid, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(lst) <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    counts = Counter(lst)\n    for num, count in counts.items():\n        if num < 0:\n            return False\n        if count > 2:\n            return False\n\n    for i in range(len(lst) - 1):\n        if lst[i] > lst[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n    return True\n```"}
