{"task_id": "HumanEval/133", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\nclass InvalidInputError(Exception):\n    \"\"\"Custom exception for invalid input scenarios.\n    Provides more context than generic Python exceptions.\n    \"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, message: str):\n        super().__init__(message)\n        self.message = message\n\ndef sum_squares(lst):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of squares of numbers in a list, rounding each number up to the nearest integer first.\n    Raises InvalidInputError if input is not a list or contains non-numeric elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(lst, list):\n        raise InvalidInputError(\"Input must be a list.\")\n\n    squared_values = []\n    for item in lst:\n        if not isinstance(item, (int, float)):\n            raise InvalidInputError(\"All elements in the list must be numbers.\")\n        \n        # Round up, then square.\n        squared_values.append(int(math.ceil(item)) ** 2)\n\n    return sum(squared_values)\n```"}
