{"task_id": "HumanEval/141", "solution": "```python\ndef file_name_check(file_name):\n    \"\"\"Create a function which takes a string representing a file's name, and returns\n    'Yes' if the the file's name is valid, and returns 'No' otherwise.\n    A file's name is considered to be valid if and only if all the following conditions \n    are met:\n    - There should not be more than three digits ('0'-'9') in the file's name.\n    - The file's name contains exactly one dot '.'\n    - The substring before the dot should not be empty, and it starts with a letter from \n    the latin alphapet ('a'-'z' and 'A'-'Z').\n    - The substring after the dot should be one of these: ['txt', 'exe', 'dll']\n    Examples:\n    file_name_check(\"example.txt\") # => 'Yes'\n    file_name_check(\"1example.dll\") # => 'No' (the name should start with a latin alphapet letter)\n    \"\"\"\n    MAX_DIGITS_IN_FILENAME = 3\n    ALLOWED_EXTENSIONS = ['txt', 'exe', 'dll']\n\n    # FR3: The file name must contain exactly one dot.\n    if file_name.count('.') != 1:\n        return 'No'\n\n    # Split the file name into prefix and extension.\n    parts = file_name.split('.', 1)\n    prefix = parts[0]\n    extension = parts[1]\n\n    # FR4: The substring before the dot must not be empty and start with a letter.\n    if not prefix or not prefix[0].isalpha():\n        return 'No'\n\n    # FR5: The substring after the dot must be one of the allowed extensions.\n    if extension not in ALLOWED_EXTENSIONS:\n        return 'No'\n\n    # FR2: The file name must not contain more than three digits.\n    digit_count = sum(1 for char in file_name if char.isdigit())\n    if digit_count > MAX_DIGITS_IN_FILENAME:\n        return 'No'\n\n    # If all checks pass, the file name is valid.\n    return 'Yes'\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/140", "solution": "```python\nimport re\n\ndef fix_spaces(text: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Replaces spaces in a string: single spaces become underscores,\n    and sequences of more than two consecutive spaces become a hyphen.\n    Examples: \"Example 1\" -> \"Example_1\", \" Example   3\" -> \"_Example-3\".\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(text, str):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a string.\")\n\n    # Replace sequences of 3 or more spaces with a single hyphen.\n    # This must be done first to preserve two-space sequences.\n    modified_text = re.sub(r' {3,}', '-', text)\n\n    # Replace all remaining single spaces with underscores.\n    # This also converts two consecutive spaces into two underscores.\n    modified_text = re.sub(r' ', '_', modified_text)\n\n    return modified_text\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/142", "solution": "```python\nclass MathUtils:\n    \"\"\"Provides static utility methods for checking if a number is a multiple of another. Stateless helper for arithmetic checks.\"\"\"\n    @staticmethod\n    def is_multiple(number: int, factor: int) -> bool:\n        return number % factor == 0\n\nclass ListProcessor:\n    \"\"\"Encapsulates logic for transforming list elements based on index rules and summing them. It uses MathUtils for index checks.\"\"\"\n    def __init__(self, math_utils: MathUtils):\n        self.math_utils = math_utils\n\n    def process_and_sum(self, data_list: list[int]) -> int:\n        processed_list = list(data_list)\n        for i, value in enumerate(processed_list):\n            if self.math_utils.is_multiple(i, 3):\n                processed_list[i] = value * value\n            elif self.math_utils.is_multiple(i, 4):\n                processed_list[i] = value * value * value\n            # else: value remains unchanged\n        return sum(processed_list)\n\ndef sum_squares(lst: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    This function processes a list of integers, applying transformations based on index rules, and returns their sum.\n    Elements at multiples of 3 are squared, while elements at multiples of 4 (but not 3) are cubed; others remain unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    math_utils = MathUtils()\n    processor = ListProcessor(math_utils)\n    return processor.process_and_sum(lst)\n```"}
