{"task_id": "HumanEval/146", "solution": "```python\ndef specialFilter(nums):\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts numbers in an array that are greater than 10 and have odd first and last digits.\n    Float values are truncated to integers for digit extraction.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    def _get_first_digit(num_val):\n        \"\"\"Extracts the first digit of a number, ignoring its sign. Handles floats by truncating.\"\"\"\n        s_num = str(abs(int(num_val)))\n        return int(s_num[0])\n\n    def _get_last_digit(num_val):\n        \"\"\"Extracts the last digit of a number. Handles floats by truncating.\"\"\"\n        s_num = str(int(num_val))\n        return int(s_num[-1])\n\n    def _is_odd(digit_val):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a given digit is odd.\"\"\"\n        return digit_val % 2 != 0\n\n    count = 0\n    for num in nums:\n        try:\n            if not num > 10:\n                continue\n\n            first_digit = _get_first_digit(num)\n            if not _is_odd(first_digit):\n                continue\n\n            last_digit = _get_last_digit(num)\n            if not _is_odd(last_digit):\n                continue\n\n            count += 1\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            # Skips non-numeric elements or those causing conversion errors, per FR1 error handling.\n            continue\n    return count\n```"}
