{"task_id": "HumanEval/150", "solution": "```python\nimport math\n\ndef x_or_y(n, x, y):\n    \"\"\"A simple program which should return the value of x if n is\n    a prime number and should return the value of y otherwise.\"\"\"\n\n    # Validate 'n' for type and value as per specifications.\n    if not isinstance(n, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'n' must be an integer.\")\n    if n <= 1:\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'n' must be greater than 1 for primality test.\")\n\n    is_n_prime = True\n\n    # Implement primality test logic.\n    if n == 2:\n        is_n_prime = True\n    elif n % 2 == 0:\n        is_n_prime = False\n    else:\n        # Check for divisibility from 3 up to sqrt(n), stepping by 2.\n        for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1, 2):\n            if n % i == 0:\n                is_n_prime = False\n                break\n    \n    if is_n_prime:\n        return x\n    else:\n        return y\n```"}
