{"task_id": "HumanEval/152", "solution": "```python\ndef compare(game, guess):\n    \"\"\"Determines how far off each guess was from the actual game score.\n    Returns 0 for correct guesses and the absolute difference for incorrect ones.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(game, list) or not isinstance(guess, list):\n        raise TypeError(\"Inputs 'game' and 'guess' must be lists.\")\n    \n    if len(game) != len(guess):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input arrays 'game' and 'guess' must be of equal length.\")\n\n    differences = []\n    for i in range(len(game)):\n        try:\n            game_score = int(game[i])\n            guess_score = int(guess[i])\n        except (ValueError, TypeError):\n            raise ValueError(f\"Elements at index {i} must be integers.\")\n\n        if game_score == guess_score:\n            differences.append(0)\n        else:\n            differences.append(abs(game_score - guess_score))\n    \n    return differences\n```"}
{"task_id": "HumanEval/153", "solution": "```python\ndef Strongest_Extension(class_name, extensions):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the strongest extension from a list based on CAP - SM strength calculation.\n    Returns the result formatted as 'ClassName.StrongestExtensionName'.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _calculate_strength(extension_name):\n        \"\"\"\n        Calculates the strength of an extension name (CAP - SM).\n        CAP is uppercase count, SM is lowercase count.\n        \"\"\"\n        cap_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'A' <= char <= 'Z')\n        sm_count = sum(1 for char in extension_name if 'a' <= char <= 'z')\n        return cap_count - sm_count\n\n    if not extensions:\n        # Handles the case where the extensions list is empty.\n        return f\"{class_name}.\"\n\n    max_strength = -float('inf')\n    strongest_extension_name = \"\"\n\n    # Iterates through extensions to find the one with the highest strength.\n    for ext in extensions:\n        current_strength = _calculate_strength(ext)\n        # Updates if a strictly stronger extension is found; handles ties by selecting the first.\n        if current_strength > max_strength:\n            max_strength = current_strength\n            strongest_extension_name = ext\n    \n    # Formats and returns the final string.\n    return f\"{class_name}.{strongest_extension_name}\"\n```"}
