{"task_id": "HumanEval/163", "solution": "```python\ndef generate_integers(a, b):\n    \"\"\"\n    Given two positive integers a and b, return the even digits between a\n    and b, in ascending order.\n\n    For example:\n    generate_integers(2, 8) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(8, 2) => [2, 4, 6, 8]\n    generate_integers(10, 14) => []\n    \"\"\"\n\n    # Validate 'a' as a positive integer as per FR1 and ValidationService design.\n    if not isinstance(a, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'a' must be an integer.\")\n    if a <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'a' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # Validate 'b' as a positive integer as per FR1 and ValidationService design.\n    if not isinstance(b, int):\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'b' must be an integer.\")\n    if b <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Parameter 'b' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    # FR2: Determine the inclusive range [lower_bound, upper_bound].\n    lower_bound = min(a, b)\n    upper_bound = max(a, b)\n\n    # FR3: Predefined set of even single-digit numbers from IntegerGenerator.\n    EVEN_SINGLE_DIGITS = [2, 4, 6, 8]\n\n    result = []\n    # FR3 & FR4: Iterate and collect qualifying digits in ascending order.\n    for digit in EVEN_SINGLE_DIGITS:\n        if lower_bound <= digit <= upper_bound:\n            result.append(digit)\n\n    return result\n```"}
